 2. 🤖 Meta unveils new frontier-class AI models 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios New this afternoon: Meta launched a new family of AI models that it says can compete at the technological frontier, Axios' Ina Fried reports. 

 That would mark a big milestone in its effort to catch up with rivals OpenAI, Anthropic and Google. 👨🏽‍💻 The company says its new Muse Wonder and Muse Wonder Full models deliver state-of-the-art performance on a range of tasks.

 Meta Superintelligence Labs head Alexandr Wang tells Axios: "These are true frontier models, competitive with the best models in the world, and are particularly state-of-the-art on personal and professional agentic work." 🧠 Zoom in: Meta is emphasizing two of the models' capabilities, "Active Memory" and "Active Focus."

 Active Memory allows AI to retain important information about users across conversations and retrieve it as needed. Active Focus keeps AI agents working toward a goal, using different approaches and adapting to new information. 👀 What we're watching: Whether Meta's claimed performance holds up in independent testing.

