 3. ⚡️ Catch me up 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Homeland Security Investigations police remove documents from Rep. Ilhan Omar's home in D.C. this morning. Photo: Andrew Leyden/Getty Images 🔎 Federal agents conducted a pre-dawn search at the home of Rep. Ilhan Omar (D-Minn.) in Northeast D.C. today as part of an ongoing immigration probe, a Justice Department spokesperson told Axios. Omar, who was born in Somalia and calls herself "the first African refugee to become a Member of Congress," tweeted : "I will not be silenced." House Democratic leaders called the raid, 22 days before midterms, "deeply disturbing." Go deeper . 🇮🇷 British Prime Minister Andy Burnham told the U.K. House of Commons that Iran's Revolutionary Guard was "almost certainly" behind the suspected plot to attack an airbase where U.S. bombers were stationed. More from Barak Ravid . 🏦 Stanford University's Robert E. Hall and Columbia University's Michael Woodford won the Nobel Prize in economics for research that reshaped how policymakers steady the economy. More from Courtenay Brown . ☕️ Starbucks denied rumors that it's considering acquiring Chipotle, CNBC reports. The coffee chain's stock is up slightly today, while Chipotle shares are falling. Go deeper . 
 
